  "id": "Compound::DB00346 - Gene::146",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Alfuzosin and Adra1d, mediated through the alpha-adrenergic antagonist class. Alfuzosin and Silodosin, both alpha-adrenergic antagonists, are linked to Intraoperative Floppy Iris Syndrome, which is caused by Tamsulosin, another alpha-adrenergic antagonist. This indicates that Alfuzosin and its analogs may share a common mechanism of action involving the alpha-adrenergic receptor, leading to the observed effects. The evidence supports the idea that Alfuzosin binds to Adra1d, as inferred from the binding of Tamsulosin to Adra1d, and that this binding is part of the broader class of alpha-adrenergic antagonists. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, with Alfuzosin and its related compounds likely influencing Adra1d through a shared biological pathway. The evidence is robust but does not exclude the possibility of additional mechanisms or variations in the interaction.",
